### The Triage Lesson

If the team had run the Suitability Assessment before building and respected the M-Regulatory placement, the SOW omission would have surfaced as a Map-extension condition before code was written. The Verifier Node would have caught the evidence gap at Stage IV. The audit log would have made the failure trivially diagnosable rather than requiring forensic reconstruction. The Stage III, IV, and V failures all trace back to a pragmatic upstream cause (Map omission) compounded by missing attestation surfaces. The diagnostic protocol can locate this after the fact; the suitability assessment can prevent it.

